## Frappe client (`frappe` piece)

`apps/__NAME__/src/app.ts` wires `createApp({ frappe: … })`: the
`FrappeProvider` mounts when `FRAPPE_ENABLED=1` and talks to the Frappe server
at `FRAPPE_URL` (both are `public` env keys in `packages/config/config.json`,
loaded from `.env` — start from `.env.example`). This piece brings no server
of its own; add the `frappe-bench` piece for a dev server in docker.

### Running against fixtures, with no server

`createApp` takes a fixture corpus, so the app runs with no server and no
network. Hand `frappe.fixtures` a `FixtureProvider` in
`apps/__NAME__/src/app.ts`:

```ts
import { createApp } from "@repo/core";
import { InMemoryFixtureProvider } from "@repo/frappe";
import { themeConfig } from "@package/themes";

const fixtures = new InMemoryFixtureProvider({
  Customer: [
    { name: "CUST-0001", doctype: "Customer", customer_name: "Acme" },
    { name: "CUST-0002", doctype: "Customer", customer_name: "Globex" },
  ],
});

export const { AppProvider, useAppConfig, withApp } = createApp({
  theme: themeConfig,
  frappe: { fixtures },
});
```

`FrappeTable`, `FrappeList` and the other collection-backed components then
read from the corpus. Writes land in it too, so create/update/delete work for
the session.

Two things follow from setting `fixtures`:

- the provider mounts without `FRAPPE_ENABLED=1`, and
- `baseURL` takes no fallback. Only a `baseURL` you pass explicitly is used,
  so `BASE_URL` cannot quietly point fixture reads at the app's own origin.

Column labels and filter fields come from DocType metadata, which lives in
the corpus under the `DocType` doctype (the `getdoctype` shape) when you want
it:

```ts
const fixtures = new InMemoryFixtureProvider({
  DocType: [
    {
      name: "Customer",
      doctype: "DocType",
      fields: [{ fieldname: "customer_name", fieldtype: "Data", label: "Customer Name" }],
    },
  ],
  Customer: [{ name: "CUST-0001", doctype: "Customer", customer_name: "Acme" }],
});
```

Leave it out and the table still renders its rows; it just has no
metadata-derived filter fields.

To point the same app at a real Frappe server again, drop `fixtures` and set
`FRAPPE_ENABLED=1` + `FRAPPE_URL` in `.env`.
